    {
      "number": 53,
      "source_text_sha256": "21ce6c074d7aea761ab3f529483bf8653c1fb310e11df98ffcca7b29ec939829",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Vision Input",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Each image is represented as a description of m objects detected with",
        "Faster R-CNN using features from Faster R-CNN and position encodings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 54,
      "source_text_sha256": "5069dba0fdcec05a9ac31bfe297d6297b4fd5b670ea43aea7c713933266fc95b",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Transformer encoder (i.e., BERT);",
        "what does its output represent?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 55,
      "source_text_sha256": "10b2695cd8eb51e8d85086eae553ae835eb64ee6909827216dcb27ecade42c74",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Transformer encoder (i.e., BERT); represents",
        "objects with their relationships to all objects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 56,
      "source_text_sha256": "07c5b67b361a2a2d0ef9a66b0d0cef38fff0c33113121808ce80a14b48dc3ea0",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Learns cross-modality representations",
        "by aligning entities in the two modalities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 57,
      "source_text_sha256": "fd424e868681d63e2a0cd89998e662d433fc2cbebcc461e5a7a011730ce7eff6",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Two cross-attention layers are functions of the “query” and",
        "“context” vectors which are language and vision features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 58,
      "source_text_sha256": "830d26cfff4ffab3d4a2b4b39316a38b880f5cd153221f1b54c0370f3071be1f",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Output is weighted sum of context",
        "vectors, weighted by the attention scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 59,
      "source_text_sha256": "4b1b322156748d7b3d07d1f64e82a14681a74747c489a794ea4058661cb9c3f1",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Two more layers of transformer",
        "encoders (i.e., BERT)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 60,
      "source_text_sha256": "e402ce507d3e6c2210d52e3c3118b85e09a8b065f31be0fdf0fe7e21103ac4f0",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Output",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "New representation of input language sequence",
        "New representation of input detected objects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 61,
      "source_text_sha256": "4e10b44e829eba172207dda8c36d24f2e3f6ea908ec616a44c8e25a354e02bee",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Output",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Cross-modality representation is the [CLS]",
        "token appended at the start of the sentence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 62,
      "source_text_sha256": "0b83d3cce17424726a3af77cde08e5331791c2f6b27bd2d9ddc08f961a5bbd89",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Implementation Details",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Pretrained Faster R-CNN can locate 1,600 categories",
        "and only 36 object detections are kept per image",
        "L = 9",
        "R = 5 X = 5",
        "Number of layers mimics the size of BERT base of 12 layers;",
        "i.e., (5+9)/2 + 5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 63,
      "source_text_sha256": "0bb35296cec5ceeee18713652a11b1643bca904351bbc7aef48e561eff64c276",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Architecture",
        "What might be strengths and limitations of the resulting feature",
        "representations based on the architecture used?",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 64,
      "source_text_sha256": "8cc2d6a830611972b704cf432b2d29a27e6de0074b5035561333ea7760c6f1ef",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Summary of Architecture",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 65,
      "source_text_sha256": "48bff000b84abba4d3127f50a97edb246f80eb2de8f3e1607861317d3f62bb53",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Task 1 (Language)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Task used for BERT: mask 15% of input words and then predict them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 66,
      "source_text_sha256": "926aaaf3cb8edda790b535466646c337444014d882882705711a740dd6ff0540",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Task 1 (Language)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Unlike BERT, vision modality can resolve language ambiguity; e.g., shows what is being eaten"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 67,
      "source_text_sha256": "054844095783a10d62af6d1287bc234e2b49d8efee7d5a23c625d61b89df0c6b",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Tasks 2 & 3 (Vision)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Mask 15% of input objects and then predict their original feature values and categories",
        "(Goal: predict same",
        "category predicted",
        "by Faster R-CNN)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 68,
      "source_text_sha256": "7ba26b34495f386ad2f6cbbdc823c9d6058c73c577a316892ed2322d558d8147",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Tasks 2 & 3 (Vision)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Knowledge about other objects and the language should help predict masked objects",
        "(Goal: predict same",
        "category predicted",
        "by Faster R-CNN)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 69,
      "source_text_sha256": "7ecb07dd61a2b014c0194f0c0164243bc34f27d517e34c3d1d369a514a2e581d",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Tasks 4 & 5 (Both Modalities)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Task 4: predict if caption and",
        "image match, where 50% of",
        "the time captions are random",
        "A dog watching a",
        "rabbit eat a carrot"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 70,
      "source_text_sha256": "bdef81a13c9f6734e6b91c6efbe05b5aa89638d54fd3631ad2804d8905d2e66a",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Pretraining Tasks 4 & 5 (Both Modalities)",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Task 5: perform VQA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 71,
      "source_text_sha256": "dba4fd88a1441952ae9db28324d4f097133f07eefa800695794a937c374e611a",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: 5 Pretraining Tasks",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 72,
      "source_text_sha256": "06888cf9359188c4934176d26c6d324492234c832b695a82d5d7c17669cf1ab6",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: All Pretraining Task Losses Are",
        "Summed During Training",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "What might be strengths and limitations of the resulting feature",
        "representations based on the type of pretraining tasks used?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 73,
      "source_text_sha256": "3476f9d0041411d94feb0722defc6b4af2c485f2347d977437eb3ef491c773be",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Training Data for Pretraining",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "All images are from two image sets, MS COCO and Visual Genome, which",
        "were collected by scraping images from the photo-sharing website Flickr",
        "(Visual Genome includes the MS COCO images)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 74,
      "source_text_sha256": "f720b2865e92b1401f7fbbfda78906dcb886dc09f9dc30c5e3574b1e38a4b27c",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Training Data for Pretraining",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Language annotations came from 2 image captioning and 3 VQA datasets,",
        "authored by crowdworkers paid to create captions, questions, and answers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 75,
      "source_text_sha256": "9306be0dac8c66f4f04a7dc434e902f3269e11a4ae3802d7b8ffb869289c475f",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Training Data for Pretraining",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "A total of 9.18M image-sentence pairs are included for 180,000 images",
        "(questions in VQA datasets are used for the image-sentence pairs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 76,
      "source_text_sha256": "2ead98ad263f299c76e8ca0cbad6734f30cc50b29b273a3b7e1324fb7b02a69c",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Training Data for Pretraining",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "What might be strengths and limitations of the resulting feature",
        "representations based on the type of training data that is used?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 77,
      "source_text_sha256": "236e9ba82697f7cdbbc45cf2263976b59586acfbbb7d87dbcd9a9705e2592681",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Fine-Tuning Experimental Results",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "Achieved the best performance,",
        "with stronger gains over prior",
        "work for questions that lead to",
        "“binary” and “other” answers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 78,
      "source_text_sha256": "d16c0ada432fb6c33014641bf6a112e10f4f3605ec7106f919aa144d808d9e04",
      "lines": [
        "LXMERT: Fine-Tuning Experimental Results",
        "Tan and Bansal, EMNLP 2019.",
        "The representations also led to the best performance for an additional VQA dataset",
        "and a visual reasoning task (i.e., does statement describe two images or not)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 79,
      "source_text_sha256": "e3d2b325c9237156f8ed6be0dec8330a54c96040c9ce285e4ff43842a2e792b8",
      "lines": [
        "Today’s Topics",
        "• Visual question answering applications",
        "• Visual question answering datasets",
        "• Visual question answering evaluation",
        "• Mainstream challenge 2015 winner: baseline approach",
        "• Mainstream challenge 2019 winner: transformer-based approach",
        "• Programming tutorial"
      ]
    },
    {
